      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Based only on the description, it is not definitively clear if the homeowner should be concerned. While an individual walking slowly at night near a house can be routine, the combination of a dark hoodie and pausing to look at house numbers could potentially be interpreted as surveillance behavior. It would be wise to incorporate other situational data, such as elapsed time, known neighborhood patterns, or unusual duration of the activity, for a more informed assessment.",
